ue added up to $41.9 billion (computed from five filed figures), operating income to $2.6 billion and net income to $2.8 billion.","cites":["HPE.d.revenue.2024-11-01.2025-10-31","HPE.d.revenue.2024-11-01.2025-07-31","HPE.d.revenue.2025-11-01.2026-01-31","HPE.d.revenue.2026-02-01.2026-04-30","HPE.d.revenue.2026-05-01.2026-07-31","HPE.d.opinc.2024-11-01.2025-10-31","HPE.d.opinc.2024-11-01.2025-07-31","HPE.d.opinc.2025-11-01.2026-01-31","HPE.d.opinc.2026-02-01.2026-04-30","HPE.d.opinc.2026-05-01.2026-07-31","HPE.d.netinc.2024-11-01.2025-10-31","HPE.d.netinc.2024-11-01.2025-07-31","HPE.d.netinc.2025-11-01.2026-01-31","HPE.d.netinc.2026-02-01.2026-04-30","HPE.d.netinc.2026-05-01.2026-07-31"]},{"topic":"ttm","text":"Free cash flow over the same four quarters was $4.2 billion: operating cash flow of $6.7 billion less capital spending of $2.5 billion (computed from ten filed figures).","cites":["HPE.d.ocf.2024-11-01.2025-10-31","HPE.d.ocf.2024-11-01.2025-07-31","HPE.d.ocf.2025-11-01.2026-01-31","HPE.d.ocf.2025-11-01.2026-04-30","HPE.d.ocf.2025-11-01.2026-07-31","HPE.d.capex.2024-11-01.2025-10-31","HPE.d.capex.2024-11-01.2025-07-31","HPE.d.capex.2025-11-01.2026-01-31","HPE.d.capex.2025-11-01.2026-04-30","HPE.d.capex.2025-11-01.2026-07-31"]},{"topic":"pay","text":"The proxy statement filed 2026-02-11 gives the principal executive officer’s total pay for FY2025 as $23.5 million in its summary compensation table, and the “compensation actually paid” - the SEC’s measure, which revalues share awards over the year - as $30.7 million.","cites":["HPE.pay.peoTotal.2025","HPE.pay.peoPaid.2025"]},{"topic":"pay","text":"For the other named executive officers the same table gives an average of $11.8 million in total and $14.4 million actually paid.","cites":["HPE.pay.neoTotal.2025","HPE.pay.neoPaid.2025"]},{"topic":"pay","text":"The table puts the value of $100 held in the company’s shares over the years it covers at $329.00 at the end of FY2025, and $319.00 for the peer group the company chose.","cites":["HPE.pay.tsr.2025","HPE.pay.peerTsr.2025"]},{"topic":"backlog","text":"Remaining performance obligations - revenue under contract that was not yet recognised - were $10.3 billion at the end of FY2025, against $7.5 billion a year earlier. That is 30% of FY2025 revenue (computed from two filed figures).","cites":["HPE.rpo.2025","HPE.rpo.2024","HPE.revenue.2025"]},{"topic":"backlog","text":"Deferred revenue was $10.3 billion at the end of FY2025 (tagged ContractWithCustomerLiability), against $7.5 billion a year earlier.","cites":["HPE.deferred.2025","HPE.deferred.2024"]},{"topic":"people","text":"The latest annual report gives the workforce as 67,000 in its own words. FY2025 revenue works out to about $512,000 for each (computed from one filed figure and the number in that sentence).","cites":["HPE.q.employees","HPE.revenue.2025"]},{"topic":"flags","text":"The FY2025 annual report tags a goodwill impairment of $1.6 billion.","cites":["HPE.impairment.2025"]},{"topic":"debt","text":"At the end of FY2025 the balance sheet carried $5.8 billion in cash and cash equivalents, and $22.4 billion of debt as tagged (LongTermDebtAndCapitalLeaseObligations + DebtCurrent). Debt less cash was $16.6 billion (computed from three filed figures).","cites":["HPE.cash.2025","HPE.debtLong.2025","HPE.debtCurrent.2025"]}]},"fin":{"HPE":{"insiders":{"from":"2025-11-23","to":"2026-11-23","complete":true,"listed":94,"read":94,"other":0,"failed":0,"odd":0,"people":[["rahim rami","EVP, Pres GM Networking"],["Neri Antonio F","President and CEO, director"],["REINER GARY M","Director"],["Karros Kirt P","SVP, Treasurer, Corp Dev"],["Mayer Bethany","Director"],["MYERS MARIE","EVP & CFO"],["RUSSO FIDELMA","EVP, GM, Hybrid Cloud & CTO"],["MacDonald Neil B","EVP, GM, Server"],["Cox Jeremy","SVP, Controller & CTO"],["Culloty Maeve C","EVP, Pres & CEO Financial Serv"],["SCHULTZ JOHN F","EVP, COLO"],["Hobby Jean M.","Director"]],"rows":[["S",0,25555,1184228.92,"2026-11-16","2026-11-16","0